{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor promptly directed same-day emergency/surgical evaluation, safely deferred diabetes dosing to onsite clinicians, and the caregiver demonstrably reached the original hospital and transferred medications and records. However, the doctor never completed the authored comprehensive red-flag elicitation, did not clarify several sick-day variables before the handoff, and omitted key waiting-period wound protections such as off-loading, clean/dry dressing care, and avoiding manipulation. These are minor/moderate responsibility-chain omissions rather than serious errors because the conservative emergency pathway was executed, so the deterministic cap is grade 2.",
